🇺🇸 It's time to stop calling it "birthright citizenship." The debate isn't about rights. It's about whether a loophole in the law can be used to grant automatic citizenship simply because a child is born on U.S. soil.

The 14th Amendment was written to secure citizenship for newly freed slaves, not to incentivize illegal immigration or birth tourism.

@RogerSeverino_ is Vice President of Economic and Domestic Policy at The Heritage Foundation

